{#
    The page a rendered document sits in. One layout; what changes is the body.

    A manual page is a column beside a rail, held to a measure. A landing page
    is a run of full-bleed bands with no rail — there is nothing to navigate on
    the way in. Both carry the same head, the same bar and the same footer, and
    `structure/document.html.twig` decides which body by the page's own
    `:layout:` field.

    `soul.js` is deferred and optional: the colour of a code block is already
    in the markup the server wrote, and every element here upgrades markup that
    reads without it. A reader with no JavaScript loses the copy button, the
    search field and the fold in the rail — not the page.
#}
{#- Where the site root is, from here: `renderLink` resolves a document
    relative to the page being rendered, so the path to `index` minus its
    filename is the prefix everything at the root needs. Set before the head,
    because the head needs it too — the drop-in is copied into the output
    rather than parsed from the source, so `asset()` cannot see it. -#}
{%- set root = renderLink('/index') == '#' ? '' : renderLink('/index')|replace({'index.html': ''}) -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{% include "structure/head.html.twig" %}
{%~ block head %}
{%~ endblock %}
</head>
<body class="sds-app">
<div class="sds-shell">
    {% include "structure/header.html.twig" %}

{%~ block main %}
{%~ endblock %}

    {% include "structure/footer.html.twig" %}
</div>

</body>
</html>
